  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amit Kumar Mangal vs State Of M.P on 16 September, 2019 Author: Anand Pathak Bench: Anand Pathak 1 Mcrc-4766-2013 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Mcrc-4766-2013 (Amit Kumar Mangal Vs State Of M.P) 18 Gwalior, Dated : 16-09-2019",
    "facts": "The present petition under Section 482 of Cr.P.C. has been preferred by the petitioner for quashment of criminal case No. 1016/2008 pending before JMFC, Vidisha under Section 2(i)7(1) and 16(1)(a)(i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act as well as for quashment of order dated 18/6/2008; whereby, cognizance has been taken by the trial Court.",
    "arguments": "Counsel for the petitioner pressed for stay over proceedings of the trial Court as according to him, trial Court is likely to pronounce the judgment soon. Learned counsel for the State opposed the prayer by submitting that if trial Court is pronouncing the judgment then it would be in the fitness of things that judgment be passed finally as petitioner would have remedy of filing the appeal. Looking to the nature of controversy, prayer for interim relief deserves to be rejected.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Counsel for the petitioner pressed for stay over proceedings of the trial Court as according to him, trial Court is likely to pronounce the judgment soon. Learned counsel for the State opposed the prayer by submitting that if trial Court is pronouncing the judgment then it would be in the fitness of things that judgment be passed finally as petitioner would have remedy of filing the appeal.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Looking to the nature of controversy, prayer for interim relief deserves to be rejected.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
